# Sigarda's Aid: "You may cast Aura and Equipment spells as though they had flash" (CR 307.5, 702.8), and a bestowed spell
# is an Aura enchantment spell, not a creature spell (CR 702.103b). In Bot2's main phase Bot1 may cast Springheart Nantuko
# bestowed on Llanowar Elves: the permission reads the Aura it would be on the stack. Cast as itself, an enchantment
# creature, it is no Aura and keeps sorcery speed, so before the bestowed cast the plain cast is refused (`Ability: #1` picks
# the cast for its mana cost) beside the bestowed one that is then taken.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Sigarda's Aid
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Springheart Nantuko
Mox Sapphire
Forest
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sigarda's Aid.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Springheart Nantuko.Cast(Ability: #1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Springheart Nantuko.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves; Ability: Bestow)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Springheart Nantuko.AttachedTo = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Springheart Nantuko.Types = Enchantment
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 2
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
